        config: { writable: false },
        close: { writable: false },
        closeAll: { writable: false },
        initialize: { writable: false },
        ...
        depth: {
            get: function() {
                return modalStack.length;
            }
        }

REASON
Stacking creates two needs the old API could not express: dismissing an entire stack
(for example on route change or logout) and asking how many modals are open.
closeAll() unwinds top down without animation, since animating several layers out
simultaneously has no coherent visual result. depth reports the shared stack size.

The stale `show: { writable: false }` descriptor is dropped — there has never been a
public show() method on the instance, so it was guarding a property that did not
exist. mainForm and displayForm are unchanged in shape but now read from the topmost
layer, which is identical behaviour when only one modal is open.
